.TH SQL_FILTER 1 "September 2026" "sql-sanitizer" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
sql_filter - ultra-fast, zero-ORM, injection-safe text-to-SQLite stream filter
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B sql_filter
\[\\fB-t\\fR \\fIname\\fR | \\fB--table\\fR=\\fIname\\fR\]
\[\\fB-c\\fR \\fIcategory\\fR | \\fB--category\\fR=\\fIcategory\\fR\]
\[\\fB-l\\fR \\fIlang\\fR | \\fB--lang\\fR=\\fIlang\\fR\]
\[\\fB-b\\fR \\fIsize\\fR | \\fB--batch\\fR=\\fIsize\\fR\]
\[\\fB-w\\fR | \\fB--whole\\fR\]
\[\\fB--col-doc_id\\fR=\\fIname\\fR | \\fB--col-doc-id\\fR=\\fIname\\fR\]
\[\\fB--col-lang\\fR=\\fIname\\fR\]
\[\\fB--col-category\\fR=\\fIname\\fR\]
\[\\fB--col-raw_text\\fR=\\fIname\\fR | \\fB--col-raw-text\\fR=\\fIname\\fR\]
\[\\fB--col-created_at\\fR=\\fIname\\fR | \\fB--col-created-at\\fR=\\fIname\\fR\]
\[\\fB--no-doc_id\\fR | \\fB--no-doc-id\\fR\]
\[\\fB--no-lang\\fR\]
\[\\fB--no-category\\fR\]
\[\\fB--no-raw_text\\fR | \\fB--no-raw-text\\fR\]
\[\\fB--no-created_at\\fR | \\fB--no-created-at\\fR\]
\[\\fB-h\\fR | \\fB--help\\fR\]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B sql_filter
is a high-performance streaming parser and sanitizer implemented in Bison and C99.
It reads raw text streams or structured document blocks from standard input,
strictly sanitizes untrusted inputs against SQL injection attacks, and emits optimized
SQL transactional statements directly pipeable to the
.BR sqlite3 (1)
command-line interface.
.PP
By operating at the stream level without intermediate ORM layers, runtime garbage collection,
or high-level language virtual machines (such as Python or Node.js),
.B sql_filter
enables piping massive logs, scraped corpora, and untrusted inputs directly into SQLite
database files at native wire speed with sub-megabyte resident memory consumption.
.PP
The filter automatically outputs initial database schema declarations with
Write-Ahead Logging (WAL) pragmas and bundles record insertions into automatic
transactions to achieve maximum disk write throughput.

.SH OPTIONS
.SS General Options
.TP
\\fB-t\\fR, \\fB--table\\fR \\fIname\\fR
Specify the destination SQLite table name. Defaults to
.BR raw_corpus .
.TP
\\fB-c\\fR, \\fB--category\\fR \\fIcategory\\fR
Set the default category attribute for records. Defaults to
.BR general .
.TP
\\fB-l\\fR, \\fB--lang\\fR \\fIcode\\fR
Set the default ISO language code attribute. Defaults to
.BR ja .
.TP
\\fB-b\\fR, \\fB--batch\\fR \\fIsize\\fR
Set the automatic transaction batch size (number of INSERT statements per BEGIN/COMMIT block). Defaults to
.BR 1000 .
.TP
\\fB-w\\fR, \\fB--whole\\fR
Whole-stream absorption mode. Ingests all standard input up to EOF as a single record rather than splitting line by line.
.TP
\\fB-h\\fR, \\fB--help\\fR
Display command synopsis, list all available options, and exit.

.SS Column Name Customization
Both underscore and hyphen notations are accepted for option flags.
.TP
\\fB--col-doc_id\\fR \\fIname\\fR, \\fB--col-doc-id\\fR \\fIname\\fR
Rename the identifier column. Defaults to
.BR doc_id .
.TP
\\fB--col-lang\\fR \\fIname\\fR
Rename the language code column. Defaults to
.BR lang .
.TP
\\fB--col-category\\fR \\fIname\\fR
Rename the domain category column. Defaults to
.BR category .
.TP
\\fB--col-raw_text\\fR \\fIname\\fR, \\fB--col-raw-text\\fR \\fIname\\fR
Rename the text content column. Defaults to
.BR raw_text .
.TP
\\fB--col-created_at\\fR \\fIname\\fR, \\fB--col-created-at\\fR \\fIname\\fR
Rename the timestamp column. Defaults to
.BR created_at .

.SS Column Omission Flags
When specified, the column is completely omitted from both the generated
.B CREATE TABLE
schema definition and all emitted
.B INSERT INTO
statements.
.TP
\\fB--no-doc_id\\fR, \\fB--no-doc-id\\fR
Omit the identifier column.
.TP
\\fB--no-lang\\fR
Omit the language code column.
.TP
\\fB--no-category\\fR
Omit the category column.
.TP
\\fB--no-raw_text\\fR, \\fB--no-raw-text\\fR
Omit the raw text column.
.TP
\\fB--no-created_at\\fR, \\fB--no-created-at\\fR
Omit the timestamp column.

.SH INPUT MODES
.B sql_filter
transparently supports two distinct input styles without requiring explicit mode flags:

.SS 1. Plain Stream Line Mode
Every non-empty, non-whitespace line is ingested as an individual record.
Default metadata configured via
.BR -c ,
.BR -l ,
and internal defaults are attached to each line.

.SS 2. Structured DSL Block Mode
Enclosed document blocks allow assigning per-document identifiers, language codes, and categories:
.PP
.nf
.RS
Document(id: "doc_001", lang: "en", category: "audit_log") {
Raw multi-line untrusted text goes here.
Quotes like 'hello' and attack vectors like:
'); DROP TABLE raw_corpus; --
are safely escaped without syntax breakout.
}
.RE
.fi

.SH SECURITY MODEL
.B sql_filter
enforces mathematical immunity against SQL injection vulnerabilities:
.IP 1. 4
\\fBSingle-Quote Escaping\\fR: Every single-quote character (\\f(CW'\\fR) within input payloads is converted to SQLite's literal double-quote escape sequence (\\f(CW''\\fR).
.IP 2. 4
\\fBNUL Byte Elimination\\fR: ASCII NUL bytes (\\f(CW\\0\\fR) are dropped from the output stream to thwart C-string termination truncation exploits.
.IP 3. 4
\\fBControl Character Scrubbing\\fR: ASCII control codes below \\f(CW0x20\\fR (excluding newline \\f(CW\\n\\fR, carriage return \\f(CW\\r\\fR, and horizontal tab \\f(CW\\t\\fR) are replaced with benign spaces, preventing terminal injection and driver corruption.

.SH EXAMPLES
.SS Example 1: Direct pipe to SQLite database
.PP
.nf
.RS
echo "Hello, world's data!" | ./bin/sql_filter | sqlite3 corpus.db
.RE
.fi

.SS Example 2: Column omission and custom column mapping
.PP
.nf
.RS
cat raw_log.txt | ./bin/sql_filter \\
\--table custom_logs \\
\--no-doc_id \\
\--no-lang \\
\--col-raw_text body \\
\--col-created_at inserted_at | sqlite3 corpus.db
.RE
.fi

.SS Example 3: Whole-stream absorption for large documents
.PP
.nf
.RS
./bin/sql_filter -w --table books --no-doc_id < war_and_peace.txt | sqlite3 library.db
.RE
.fi

.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Success. All input records parsed and valid SQL stream emitted.
.TP
.B 1
Fatal error encountered (such as memory allocation failure or invalid command-line arguments).

.SH SEE ALSO
.BR sqlite3 (1),
.BR bison (1),
.BR groff (1),
